      "id": "claim_9b5929af1ce44530bab3d1d6e5a21d77",
      "statement": "The Claude Code commit hook reads every form of `git commit` (`-C`, `-c`, `--opt` before it; `-a`, a pathspec, or `git add … &&` before it) and needs `jq`; while any gated file differs from HEAD it requires a gate receipt matching the worktree, refuses a staged gated file that differs from the worktree or an untracked one left out, and refuses `--no-verify` and `-n`; a public commit made while the record holds a completed spec it has not committed yet needs a matching OpenWiki receipt too, unless a waiver is in force; a commit aimed at the record itself is exempt.",
