      "id": "claim_7deb11bb36054dddaa972213c7c36033",
      "statement": "Two Claude Code hooks for the brain loop ship inside `rusty-cli` and are installed by `rusty-cli hooks install` (scripts to `~/.rusty/hooks/`, Rusty's commands added to `~/.claude/settings.json`, a stale one from another home replaced, every other entry and the file's key order kept, the file left untouched when nothing changes; `uninstall` removes only Rusty's commands, an entry going only when nothing else is left in it): in a working directory whose `.mcp.json` configures a server named `rusty`, the PreToolUse hook blocks a Write, Edit, MultiEdit or NotebookEdit under that directory until the transcript holds a `mcp__rusty__brain_ask` tool use whose result was not an error, and the Stop hook refuses a stop once (`stop_hook_active` passes the retry) when files under the directory were written and no non-error `brain_decide` or `brain_no_decision` follows; both fail open without jq or a readable transcript; a corpus test runs the shipped scripts.",
